Within the implementation sections of my project I have included the essentials sections for my: DTO, Controller, Service, Exception and Utility classes for my PA03 project.

I organized each of these in the locations where they are most relevant for better readability in between different classes and functionality between the class code sequences.

The focus of my project is to implement a RESTful Campus Resources API in Java using Spring Boot with two main DTO types: Categories and Locations. 

My project covers:
- Controller/Service/DTO pattern (no database)
- Bean Validation (`@Valid`, `@NotBlank`, `@NotNull`)
- Paging and sorting with a `PageEnvelope`
- Global exception handling with a uniform error JSON format
- Referential integrity enforcement (409 Conflict)
- Among other essential topics focused in the instructions.

In order to run it, it requires these instructions: 
## Run Instructions
1. Open the project in IntelliJ.
2. Run the main Spring Boot class (e.g., `Pa03ProjectApplication.java`).
3. The API will start on [http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080). - ex. 

